# PHP & WordPress standards

## File header

Every PHP file:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package Caas_Control
 */

declare( strict_types=1 );

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

Partials may use `defined( 'ABSPATH' ) || exit;` on one line. In partials, use full `<?php … ?>` for template helpers (`checked`, `selected`, `esc_html_e`, etc.)—do not rely on short open tags.

## Security

- Capabilities: `current_user_can( 'manage_options' )` (or tighter) before admin actions and sensitive output.
- Escape on output: `esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `esc_url`, `wp_kses_post` as appropriate.
- Sanitize on input: `sanitize_text_field`, `absint`, Settings API / `register_setting` for options.
- Nonces for forms and AJAX: `wp_nonce_field`, `check_admin_referer`, `wp_verify_nonce`.
- Never trust `$_GET` / `$_POST` / `$_REQUEST` without validation.

## i18n

Wrap user-visible strings: `__( '...', 'caas-control' )`, `_e`, `esc_html_e`, etc.

## Assets

Enqueue only when settings allow (`Caas_Control_Settings::is_enabled()` and `should_load_chaos()`) on relevant screens. Admin: plugin CSS/JS on CaaS menu pages; same admin JS/CSS on user profile screens when CaaS is enabled (tooltips on sidekick fields). Admin plugin CSS lists `dashicons` as a dependency. On CaaS settings pages, enqueue public chaos CSS when admin chaos or the behavior **preview harness** loads (`should_load_public_chaos_styles()`). Chaos JS when `should_load_admin_chaos()` passes (includes `habitat_specific_only` + block editor), or on settings-only preview with `previewHarness: true` in localized config. Pass `$this->version` for cache busting. Localize chaos with `chaos_config_for_js()` plus `context`, `isAdmin`, `sidekick`, and `previewHarness` where applicable. `caasControlAdmin` is localized only on CaaS settings screens (maintenance nonce, media upload, preview strings). Admin JS depends on chaos script when preview or full admin chaos is active. Scripts that need `wp.ajax` or DOM helpers should list dependencies (e.g. `array( 'jquery' )`) instead of an empty array.

## Settings UI helpers

- Field help: `Caas_Control_Admin::field_tip( __( '...', 'caas-control' ) )` before labels in partials and profile sidekick UI. Plain text only; escaped in the helper. Place tip before visible label text so screen readers get “More information” via the button `aria-label`.
- Global Menace: wrap the options form in `.caas-control-form` with `data-caas-cat-media-url` and `data-caas-judging-media-url` for preview sync; section headings in `.caas-control-section` inside `.caas-control-panel`.
- Chaos duration UI: range input via `duration_seconds_min()` / `max()` / `step()` and initial label from `duration_slider_display()`; styles under `.caas-control-duration-slider` in admin CSS.
- Behavior preview: `Caas_Control_Admin::behavior_preview_button( $slug )` beside timed-behavior checkboxes; `$slug` must match chaos preview handlers (`blockMouse`, `randomBlock`, etc.).

## Bundled agent media

- Resolve URLs with `Caas_Control_Settings::bundled_gpl_cat_url()`, `default_cat_media_url()`, and `judging_video_url()`—do not hard-code a single PNG path when adding bundled assets.
- Use `agent_media_is_video( $url )` before outputting scroll-post or inline sprites; prefer `Caas_Control_Public::echo_agent_sprite()` pattern (`<video muted playsinline autoplay loop>` vs `<img>`).
- Expose new bundled clips/sounds through `chaos_config_for_js()` (e.g. `judgingVideoUrl`, `meowSoundUrl`) rather than new localize blobs.

## Settings

- Do not call `update_option` for plugin toggles from random code paths; use Settings API groups in admin or extend `Caas_Control_Settings::sanitize()`.
- Feature hooks and front-end markup that are not covered by `should_load_chaos()` must still respect `Caas_Control_Settings::is_enabled()` (master off = no 404 guilt, login hiss, scroll post, etc.).
- Exception: per-user sidekick uses `update_user_meta( …, 'caas_control_sidekick', … )` via `maybe_save_sidekick()` or profile save handlers in `Caas_Control_Features`.
- New boolean settings belong in `defaults()`, `$bool_keys` (or a form-context branch), the matching admin partial, and `chaos_config_for_js()` when the front end needs them.
- `caas_enabled` is in `$bool_keys` for the `menace` form context only; sanitize always merges onto existing options so Pro saves do not wipe the master switch.
- Sanitize allowed enums: `agent` (`cat`|`custom`), `frequency_minutes` (5|10|15). `duration_seconds` uses `normalize_duration_seconds()` (5–300, step 5); legacy stored values (e.g. 10, 30) are snapped on read/save.

## Types and style

- Use typed properties and return types where the codebase already does (`: void`, `string`, etc.).
- Prefer WordPress APIs (`wpdb`, transients, cron, REST) over raw SQL or custom HTTP unless CaaS integration requires otherwise.
- Document public methods with short PHPDoc blocks; avoid noisy comments on obvious code.

## Examples

```php
// ❌ BAD
echo $_POST['api_key'];
update_option( 'key', $_POST['key'] );

// ✅ GOOD
if ( ! current_user_can( 'manage_options' ) ) {
	return;
}
$key = isset( $_POST['api_key'] ) ? sanitize_text_field( wp_unslash( $_POST['api_key'] ) ) : '';
update_option( 'caas_control_api_key', $key );
```
